1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,551
Meet video-classifier, a CPU-only proof of concept for chunker routing.

2
00:00:04,701 --> 00:00:07,325
It turns video clips into routing decisions.

3
00:00:07,833 --> 00:00:11,804
The Pareto plot shows the trade-off between accuracy and latency.

4
00:00:11,954 --> 00:00:14,752
The chosen large@8 point sits near the top-right.

5
00:00:15,267 --> 00:00:21,664
large@8 reaches 0.735 macro-F1 and 0.843 CUS.

6
00:00:21,814 --> 00:00:28,815
small@4 is close behind at 0.677 macro-F1 and 0.824 CUS.

7
00:00:29,333 --> 00:00:34,140
Predictor loads the production config, the ONNX head, and the encoder when needed.

8
00:00:34,290 --> 00:00:39,305
It extracts frames, adds motion features, and prepares the batch for inference.

9
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:44,373
Then it runs the head, computes confidence, and returns the recommended chunker.

10
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:49,823
To reproduce it, install requirements, fetch the encoder, then run evaluate,

11
00:00:49,823 --> 00:00:51,831
predict, benchmark, and pytest.

12
00:00:52,333 --> 00:00:56,989
Clone the repository and compare the faster small model with the chosen large model.
